{"query":"TanStack Start official docs create new project scaffold npm create @tanstack start latest","follow_up_questions":null,"answer":null,"images":[],"results":[{"url":"https://tanstack.com/start/v0/docs/framework/react/getting-started","title":"Getting Started | TanStack Start React Docs","content":"Remote and in-person TanStack workshops for teams that need depth.\n\nSponsorships, placements, and partner pages.\n\nReact'/%3e%3cellipse%20rx='11'%20ry='4.2'%20transform='matrix(-.5%20.8660254%20-.8660254%20-.5%200%200)'/%3e%3c/g%3e%3c/svg%3e)\nReact'/%3e%3cellipse%20rx='11'%20ry='4.2'%20transform='matrix(-.5%20.8660254%20-.8660254%20-.5%200%200)'/%3e%3c/g%3e%3c/svg%3e)\n\n# Getting Started\n\n## Start a new project#\n\n### Use TanStack Builder#\n\nThe best way to get started with TanStack Start is TanStack Builder. It's the AI-first setup flow and the easiest way to get to a working project fast.\n\n### Use the CLI#\n\nIf you'd rather scaffold locally or want a backup path, use the TanStack CLI:\n\n`npx @tanstack/cli@latest create` [...] `npx @tanstack/cli@latest create`\n\nYou'll be prompted to choose your package manager and optional add-ons like Tailwind CSS and ESLint.\n\n### Start from an example#\n\nIf you'd rather begin from a working codebase, clone one of the official examples.\n\nTo start with the Basic example:\n\n`npx gitpick TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/start-basic start-basic\ncd start-basic\nnpm install\nnpm run dev`\n\nTo use a different example, replace start-basic with one of the slugs below.\n\n#### Examples#\n\nEach example page also includes a StackBlitz preview so you can inspect it before cloning.\n\nTo clone a different example manually, replace EXAMPLE\\_SLUG below with the slug you want to use: [...] `npx gitpick TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/EXAMPLE_SLUG my-new-project\ncd my-new-project\nnpm install\nnpm run dev`\n\nIf you want to clone and deploy quickly, use the Deploy to Netlify button on an example's page.\n\n### Build from scratch#\n\nIf you want to wire everything up by hand, follow Build a project from scratch.\n\n## Migrate an existing project from another framework#\n\n## Next Steps#\n\nOnce you've created, cloned, or deployed a project, continue to the Routing guide.\n\n## Other Router Examples#\n\nIf you want Router-focused examples that are not Start-specific, these are useful references:\n\n### On this page","score":0.80844593,"raw_content":"![](https://tanstack.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=30,quality=90,format=auto/images/logos/logo-color-100.png)\n![](/images/logos/logo-black.svg)\n![](/images/logos/logo-white.svg)\n\nRemote and in-person TanStack workshops for teams that need depth.\n\nSponsorships, placements, and partner pages.\n\n![React](data:image/svg+xml,%3csvg%20viewBox='-11.5%20-10.23%2023%2020.46'%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%3e%3ccircle%20fill='%2361dafb'%20r='2.05'/%3e%3cg%20fill='none'%20stroke='%2361dafb'%3e%3cellipse%20rx='11'%20ry='4.2'/%3e%3cellipse%20rx='11'%20ry='4.2'%20transform='matrix(.5%20.8660254%20-.8660254%20.5%200%200)'/%3e%3cellipse%20rx='11'%20ry='4.2'%20transform='matrix(-.5%20.8660254%20-.8660254%20-.5%200%200)'/%3e%3c/g%3e%3c/svg%3e)\n![React](data:image/svg+xml,%3csvg%20viewBox='-11.5%20-10.23%2023%2020.46'%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%3e%3ccircle%20fill='%2361dafb'%20r='2.05'/%3e%3cg%20fill='none'%20stroke='%2361dafb'%3e%3cellipse%20rx='11'%20ry='4.2'/%3e%3cellipse%20rx='11'%20ry='4.2'%20transform='matrix(.5%20.8660254%20-.8660254%20.5%200%200)'/%3e%3cellipse%20rx='11'%20ry='4.2'%20transform='matrix(-.5%20.8660254%20-.8660254%20-.5%200%200)'/%3e%3c/g%3e%3c/svg%3e)\n\n# Getting Started\n\n## Start a new project[#](#start-a-new-project)\n\n### Use TanStack Builder[#](#use-tanstack-builder)\n\nThe best way to get started with TanStack Start is [TanStack Builder](https://tanstack.com/builder). It's the AI-first setup flow and the easiest way to get to a working project fast.\n\n### Use the CLI[#](#use-the-cli)\n\nIf you'd rather scaffold locally or want a backup path, use the TanStack CLI:\n\n`npx @tanstack/cli@latest create`\n\nYou'll be prompted to choose your package manager and optional add-ons like Tailwind CSS and ESLint.\n\n### Start from an example[#](#start-from-an-example)\n\nIf you'd rather begin from a working codebase, clone one of the official examples.\n\nTo start with the [Basic](https://github.com/TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/start-basic) example:\n\n`npx gitpick TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/start-basic start-basic\ncd start-basic\nnpm install\nnpm run dev`\n\nTo use a different example, replace start-basic with one of the slugs below.\n\n#### Examples[#](#examples)\n\nEach example page also includes a StackBlitz preview so you can inspect it before cloning.\n\nTo clone a different example manually, replace EXAMPLE\\_SLUG below with the slug you want to use:\n\n`npx gitpick TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/EXAMPLE_SLUG my-new-project\ncd my-new-project\nnpm install\nnpm run dev`\n\nIf you want to clone and deploy quickly, use the **Deploy to Netlify** button on an example's page.\n\n### Build from scratch[#](#build-from-scratch)\n\nIf you want to wire everything up by hand, follow [Build a project from scratch](/start/v0/docs/framework/react/build-from-scratch).\n\n## Migrate an existing project from another framework[#](#migrate-an-existing-project-from-another-framework)\n\n## Next Steps[#](#next-steps)\n\nOnce you've created, cloned, or deployed a project, continue to the [Routing](/start/v0/docs/framework/react/guide/routing) guide.\n\n## Other Router Examples[#](#other-router-examples)\n\nIf you want Router-focused examples that are not Start-specific, these are useful references:\n\n### On this page\n\n![Cloudflare](/assets/cloudflare-black-6Ojsn8yh.svg)\n![Cloudflare](/assets/cloudflare-white-Co-Tyjbl.svg)\n![Netlify](data:image/svg+xml,%3csvg%20width='512'%20height='209'%20viewBox='0%200%20512%20209'%20fill='none'%20xmlns=